cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "GitHub Country Classifier: Inferring a Developer's Country from Public GitHub Profiles"
abstract: >-
  A fine-tuned multilingual-e5-small classifier that infers the country (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2, 209 classes) of a GitHub
  user from the public fields of their profile (location, company, blog, email domain, Twitter handle, bio), shipped as
  a 45 MB int8 ONNX model with a trimmed vocabulary that runs locally in Node.js or the browser. Trained on 394,221
  users whose declared locations were geocoded with Nominatim; 98.8% accuracy on 46,518 held-out users with a
  location and 89.1% on 2,922 users without one, labelled by a large language model with grounded evidence.
